cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it as below, and cite the underlying data archives listed in docs/DATA_SOURCES.md."
title: "Finding Earth 2.0 in Distant Worlds"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jana"
    given-names: "Biswajit"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Biswajit1999/finding-earth-2"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-08-24
abstract: >
  A reproducible, data-driven search for potentially Earth-like worlds across
  the public astronomical archives. Ingests confirmed-planet, candidate, and
  atmospheric-spectroscopy records from the NASA Exoplanet Archive, radial
  velocities from DACE, and light curves from MAST; propagates measurement
  uncertainty by Monte Carlo; and ranks candidates on four interpretable,
  independently reported criteria (Earth similarity, conservative
  habitability, observational confidence, characterisation potential).
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - astrobiology
  - habitable zone
  - computational astrophysics
  - reproducible research
